    "title": "Is the stock market open on Good Friday? See 2026 holiday schedule",
    "text": "INVESTINGStock Market and StocksAdd TopicWhy the stock market is closed this Friday Gabe HauariUSA TODAYApril 2, 2026Updated April 3, 2026, 7:28 a.m. ETHear this story DeeperDiveBETADeeperDive is a GenAI Answer Engine built for trusted publishers. It delivers clear answers and real-time content based on what people are reading now — showcasing various stories from the usatodaydemo Network that highlight not just what happened, but why it matters. This is currently a BETA being quality assessed by human beings. Mistakes may occur. Please reference surfaced articles to validate AI summaryExplore DeeperDiveAsk USA TODAY anything When does stock market reopen after Good Friday 2026? Are banks closed on Good Friday 2026? When is Juneteenth market closure in 2026? AI Overview DeeperDive is a GenAI Answer Engine built for trusted publishers. It delivers clear answers and real-time content based on what people are reading now — showcasing various stories from the USA TODAY Network that highlight not just what happened, but why it matters. This is currently a BETA being quality assessed by human beings. Mistakes may occur. Please reference surfaced articles to validate AI summaryExplore DeeperDiveFull Summary U.S. stock markets will be closed on Good Friday, April 3, 2026, and will reopen on Monday, April 6, 2026, with the article also providing the complete 2026 market holiday schedule.United States stock markets will be closed on Friday, April 3, in observance of Good Friday, the day when those who follow the Christian faith commemorate the crucifixion and death of Jesus Christ.The Nasdaq and New York Stock Exchange will be closed on Friday and reopen on Monday, April 6. The U.S. bond market will close at noon ET Friday, according to the Securities Industry and Financial Markets Association.After shuttering for Good Friday, it will be business as usual on Wall Street until late May. The next scheduled stock market closure is on Monday, May 25, in observance of Memorial Day.US stock market 2026 holiday scheduleMarkets will be closed for the following holidays in 2026:USA TODAY Shopping: Shop sales in tech, home, fashion, beauty & more curated by our editors.Good Friday: Friday, April 3Memorial Day: Monday, May 25Juneteenth: Friday, June 19Independence Day: Friday, July 3Labor Day: Monday, Sept. 7Thanksgiving: Thursday, Nov. 26 (markets will also close at 1 p.m. ET on Nov. 25)Christmas: Friday, Dec. 25 (markets will also close at 1 p.m. ET on Dec. 24)Gabe Hauari is a national trending news reporter at USA TODAY. You can follow him on X @GabeHauari or email him at Gdhauari@gannett.com.by Taboolaby TaboolaSponsored LinksSponsored LinksPromoted LinksPromoted LinksAd Content12 Things To Cut When Living On RetirementGreensproutUndoMissouri Banks Offering 4%+ Interest RatesRateZip.comSave NowUndoHere's What Home Insurance Should Really Cost (Check Zip Code)OTTO InsuranceUndoCardiologist: The Morning Habit That Burns Fat After 50Diet-mastersUndoHere’s What a Fully Equipped Stairlift Should Cost You in 2026HomeBuddyUndoThe Average Walk-In Shower Cost in 2026Kohler ShowersLearn MoreUndoFeatured Weekly AdMore StoriesPresident Donald Trump shares new Jesus AI image in Truth Social postnewsUndoIn-N-Out is opening new locations in 4 states. See where.moneyUndo12 Things To Cut When Living On Retirement IncomeGreensprout | AdAdUndo Keep on readingPresident Donald Trump shares new Jesus AI image in Truth Social postThe latest post shows an AI image of Trump embraced by Jesus with an American flag in the background.USA TODAYUndoIn-N-Out is opening new locations in 4 states. See where.The burger chain has committed to a slow but steady expansion in recent years, opening locations in new states.USA TODAYUndo'Diff'rent Strokes' actor files for divorce from wife after 3 yearsActor Todd Bridges has officially filed for divorce from his wife, Bettijo B. Hirschi, three months after revealing their split.USA TODAYUndoJenna Bush Hager shocked after